        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/NJ/Hunterdon_County/Clinton_Township/Annandale_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1852 a station, tavern, and general store sprang up at Clinton Station, forming the nucleus around which Annandale grew.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/NJ/Hunterdon_County/Clinton_Township/Annandale_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Annandale’s historic district, with tree‑lined streets and preserved 19th‑century buildings, earned a spot on the National Register in 1994.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annandale%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Annandale once shipped lime, milk, coal, lumber, and peaches, making it a bustling rural service center rivaling nearby Clinton.",
